# The builder stage does `COPY . .`, so anything not listed here is baked into
# an image layer. Two of these are not merely wasteful:
#
#   .env*          — secrets. A layer is readable by anyone who can pull the
#                    image, and deleting the file in a later layer does not
#                    remove it from the earlier one.
#   node_modules   — host-built native modules. argon2 and sharp are compiled
#                    against the host's libc; copying Windows/glibc builds over
#                    the image's musl ones produces a container that builds
#                    fine and then fails at runtime.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
.next
out
build
dist

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local user content and generated output — the container has its own.
public/uploads
.mail-outbox
.tmp-verify
coverage
playwright-report
test-results

npm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode
.idea

# Docs and specs are not needed to run the app.
docs
README.md
